---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import { IMAGES } from '../../data/site';
import RazorpayDonate from '../../components/RazorpayDonate.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Us — GWE NGO INDIA"
  description="Glorious Women Empowerment (GWE) NGO India — registered in 1998, working for the empowerment of women and development of children in Kurnool and Kadapa Districts, Andhra Pradesh."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>About Us</h1>
        <p>Seven women. One passion for social service. Serving communities since 1998.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <img src={IMAGES.about} alt="About Glorious Women Empowerment" loading="lazy" />
        <p>
          In the year 1998, we, seven women, having passion in social service formed an organization
          by name "Glorious Women Empowerment". We are all women members and belong to backward and
          downtrodden communities. Our society was registered and started activities for the
          upliftment of the quality of life of the downtrodden communities particularly women and
          children. We focus women and children but do activities to other vulnerable,
          disadvantaged, deprived sections, who are poor and in need of help and assistance. We have
          compassion towards the problems of the poor and would like to do something for their
          empowerment. We understood that lack of knowledge and awareness is the main reason for all
          the problems of human beings. We felt the fruits of development are not reaching to the
          downtrodden communities.
        </p>
        <p>
          We would like to take up social economic, health, educational, agricultural, rural
          development and cultural activities for transformation of the society. That is why, we
          have established this society. We have service minded EC Members, dedicated staff and
          committed volunteers. We have interest, will and pleasure to take up welfare and
          developmental activities for the needy sections of the society. GWE NGO in Andhra Pradesh
          is committed to the empowerment of women and development of Children. Presently it is
          working in Kurnool and Kadapa Districts, in the coming years would like to expand its
          activities to the Ananthapur, Chittoor Districts of Andhra Pradesh. Our main of
          streamlining welfare services for the disadvantaged sections of society.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since its inception the GWE NGO is a major catalyst of social empowerment, it provides
          opportunities to women to acquire education and skills and to overcome the obstacles they
          face in their family and community. Glorious Women Empowerment is achieving its targets by
          rising online and offline donations through individual philanthropist, corporate social
          responsibility from India and abroad. You can also make online donations to our GWE NGO
          India through Paypal credit card and secure online payment gateway. All donations to
          Glorious Women Empowerment is tax deductible under 80G Income Tax Exemption Act. You will
          get a tax receipt and purpose of donation utilization after receiving money from you. You
          will receive feedback utilization of the amount for specific purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          So please donate generously to our Non Government Organization with your credit card,
          debit card and net banking with secure online payment gateway. Glorious Women Empowerment
          NGO is registered in the year 1998 under the Societies Registration Act, XXI of 1860,
          vide Regd.No. 414/1998.
        </p>
        <RazorpayDonate />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Compliance / Credentials and Legal Certificates of the NGO in Andhra Pradesh</h2>
        <p>
          As part of Good Governance, the GWE NGO India is maintaining following standards and
          filing the returns as per the societies act &amp; credibility alliance to maintain as good
          and credible NGO among several Best Indian NGOs. GWE NGO is growing nonprofit organization
          in Andhra Pradesh, which is working for the economically disadvantaged people to eradicate
          the poverty.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>The Executive Committee Members for the year 2022–2023</h2>
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>S.No.</th><th>Name</th><th>Designation</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>01</td><td>Ms. R.G. Deepika</td><td>President</td></tr>
            <tr><td>02</td><td>Ms. B. Kumari</td><td>Vice President</td></tr>
            <tr><td>03</td><td>Ms. M.D. Muneswaramma</td><td>Secretary</td></tr>
            <tr><td>04</td><td>Ms. P. Sumalatha</td><td>Joint Secretary</td></tr>
            <tr><td>05</td><td>Ms. B. Mounika</td><td>Treasurer</td></tr>
            <tr><td>06</td><td>Ms. M. Mani</td><td>Executive Member</td></tr>
            <tr><td>07</td><td>Ms. G. Gouramma</td><td>Executive Member</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          The executive committee members are belongs to dalits, working in different vocations for
          their family sustenance and working for the needy communities irrespective of caste, creed
          and religion.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Staff of the Organization</h2>
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>S.No.</th><th>Name of the Staff</th><th>Designation</th><th>Remuneration p.a.</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>01</td><td>Ms. Jayalakshmi</td><td>Project Coordinator</td><td>Rs. 24,000</td></tr>
            <tr><td>02</td><td>Ms. Rathamma</td><td>Community Organizer</td><td>Rs. 24,000</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>No. of paid volunteers: Nil &nbsp;·&nbsp; No. of un-paid volunteers: 17</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
